<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00N5">Notation <span data-tag="00N5">2.4.7.6</span>.</a> Let $W$ be a Coxeter group with identity element $1$. We let $M_0(W)$ denote the free monoid generated by the set $W \setminus \{ 1\} $. We will identify the elements of $M_0(W)$ with finite sequences $\overrightarrow {w} = ( w_1, w_2, \ldots , w_ n )$, where each $w_{i}$ is an element of $W \setminus \{ 1\} $. We will say that <em>$\overrightarrow {v}$ is a refinement of $\overrightarrow {w}$</em> if there exists a strictly increasing sequence of integers $0 = i_0 &lt; i_1 &lt; \cdots &lt; i_ n = m$ having the property that </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  w_ j = v_{ i_{j-1} + 1 } v_{ i_{j-1} + 2} \cdots v_{ i_ j } \]
</div>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \ell (w_ j) = \ell (v_{ i_{j-1} + 1 }) + \ell ( v_{ i_{j-1} + 2}) + \cdots + \ell ( v_{ i_ j } ) \]
</div>
<p> for $1 \leq j \leq n$. We write $\overrightarrow {v} \preceq \overrightarrow {w}$ to indicate that $\overrightarrow {v}$ is a refinement of $\overrightarrow {w}$. Then $\preceq $ determines a partial ordering on the set $M_0(W)$. We denote the nerve of this partially ordered set by $M_{\bullet }(W)$. Note that the multiplication on $M_0(W)$ (given by concatenation) endows $M_{\bullet }(W)$ with the structure of a simplicial monoid. </p>
</article>
